(TIM-16 - every Wait and Sleep spelling the manual lists parses and runs:
 singular and plural, seconds and milliseconds, `Wait` and `Sleep for`.
 The last two lines are not in the manual: `for` turns out to be optional
 after either verb (TIM-49), so `Sleep 4 milliseconds.` and
 `Wait for 5 milliseconds.` both compile.
 Also covers: TIM-17, TIM-18, TIM-19, TIM-49.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-16.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   every documented spelling ran
